      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "BCR-ABL inhibition made molecularly targeted cancer therapy a compelling clinical reality and changed the outlook for chronic myeloid leukemia.",
        "attribution": "The proposed names cover inhibitor development, clinical translation, and subsequent mechanistic and therapeutic validation, but important precursor contributions complicate a three-person allocation.",
        "maturity": "Long-term clinical outcomes and the general influence on precision oncology are well established.",
